      "definition": "all scored rows minus the 50,000-doc validation holdout (SeedSequence(42).spawn(8)[0]); the 5M analysis sample is not excluded"
    },
    "scorer_training_data": "The ModernBERT score is a Ridge head fit on 50,427 Claude-labelled documents (49,998 from DCLM-RefinedWeb); every one of those was removed from the pool before scoring (the 50,838-row first-4000-character match removal), so 0 are in any corpus. The ~5M analysis sample was not used to fit the head and was NOT removed (4,997,471 docs remain); each new selection holds it at its pool rate (5.00%), as does Quality-Base. Kept for comparability with the original 1.5B universe. Benchmark contamination was not tested. See reports/GLOBAL_TOP10B_SELECTION_REPORT.md \u00a72b.",
    "rules": {
